feat(attention): pd attention — harness-agent mailbox aggregator (#169)

* feat(attention): pd attention — harness-agent mailbox aggregator

PD has had broadcast plumbing (inbox, /msg channels, tuples) but harness
agents (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI) don't poll any of it on each
turn. Senders write to a black hole; receivers never read.

This is the verb half of the fix. One call returns 'everything new for this
agent' with a stable JSON schema, marks it seen on fetch (per-message markRead
on inbox so messages beyond the limit are NOT silently consumed; per-channel
cursor advance in a new attention_subscriptions table). --peek leaves cursors
in place.

Surfaces:
  - lib/attention.ts                  composer
  - routes/attention.ts               GET /attention, POST /attention/subscribe
                                      POST /attention/unsubscribe,
                                      GET /attention/subscriptions
  - cli/commands/attention.ts         pd attention [--json|--peek|--limit N|
                                      --subscribe CH|--unsubscribe CH|
                                      --subscriptions]
  - .claude/settings.json             SessionStart hook pins output into prompt
  - AGENTS.md § Port Daddy First      pd attention as first command of every session

Tests: 11 unit covering empty state, inbox mark-read, channel cursor advance,
peek semantics, sort order, limit-with-remaining accounting, idempotent
subscribe, per-agent scope, input validation. Live-daemon smoke confirmed
end-to-end. All 5828 unit tests pass.

mcp-parity: attention is in MCP_EXEMPT_FEATURES. Exposing as an MCP tool
inverts the dependency — the model would have to call it mid-turn, which is
exactly the polling problem this is supposed to remove. SessionStart hook is
the correct invocation surface.

